<section class="container" style="padding-block:4rem 2rem;max-width:760px;">
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Piasten produces chocolates and confectionery for the German market and for export markets, a considerable share of it as private labels for retail partners. Most of these brands are not advertised in the classic sense. The packaging is therefore the only medium through which the brand reaches the end consumer.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Accordingly high are the demands on packaging design: it has to work as a self-seller, triggering the purchase at the shelf without accompanying advertising. For Piasten, Lünstroth develops brands, range structures and packaging to this end – nationally, for export and for retailer brands.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 3rem;max-width:760px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A sales test before production starts</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Before a design goes into production, Lünstroth tests its sales impact with test procedures it developed itself. This reduces the risk on printing plates, tooling and first print runs. The results also serve as the basis for arguments in listing negotiations with retail.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:760px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Trademark law and labelling for export packaging</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Packaging for several countries has to meet the respective European and international labelling requirements. Competition and trademark law matter just as much: if a pack is perceived as an imitation of a competitor's product, a cease-and-desist letter looms. Even an unjustified one can strain listings and supply relationships.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Lünstroth therefore develops the brands with the different national trademark systems in mind and checks the likelihood of confusion during the design phase. <a href="/en/services/retail-listing/" style="color:var(--accent);">More on the retail listing meeting →</a></p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:1100px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Warner Hudson: an independent brand with several product lines</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;max-width:760px;">Warner Hudson is an independent brand, produced by Piasten, and was launched in international markets. A single brand mark – crest symbol and lettering – links the product lines Finest Composition, Finest Assorted Chocolates and Cherries in Brandy.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:2rem;max-width:760px;">Colour, typography and look vary within this framework. This allows the brand to be used for different price levels, markets and seasons without losing recognisability. The product names are trilingual throughout.</p>
